# The full scored candidate pool, written alongside the shortlist.
#
# Regenerable from the seed list, so it is machine output rather than project
# content — the same reason data/review/upcoming.md is ignored. Committing a
# derived snapshot puts something in the repository that contradicts its source
# the moment the source changes, and a later reader cannot tell which is current.
#
# It exists because discarding it was a real loss: the first run scored 139
# candidates and kept 12, and the other 127 were only ever a number in a log
# line. Keeping the pool on disk means a later session can pick from it without
# a fresh network run, which matters when the proxy path drops a third of
# requests.
candidates_*.csv

